Project Overview

This project presents a Multi-Objective Distribution Network Reconfiguration (DNR) approach using the Barber Optimization Algorithm (BOA). The objective is to improve the operational efficiency of radial distribution systems by simultaneously:

Reducing real power losses
Improving bus voltage profile
Maintaining network radiality

The proposed approach is evaluated on the IEEE 33-Bus, IEEE 69-Bus, and IEEE 118-Bus benchmark distribution systems and compared with several well-known optimization techniques. The paper reports that BOA provides competitive loss reduction, improved voltage stability, and faster convergence across these benchmark systems.
